From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HourlySword <hourlysword.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:15:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] FunKey S: drawing at the picture's size, faster game code,
 shorter room entries

Measured on the console with a whole-system profile (the game's CPU time per tick 27.5 -> 20.5 ms):

- The software renderer draws the stage at the picture's size (240x180 for 363x272) instead of at the stage's size
  shrunk at the end: shapes and texts rasterized at their size on screen, the game's stage-sized BitmapData drawn
  1:1 from copies shrunk by area averaging, made again only when they change. Drawing a picture in the floors
  14-16 ms -> 7-8 ms, the title 31 -> 17 ms. (Blending and scaling were bound by memory traffic, not arithmetic.)
  ISAAC_SOFT_STAGERES=1 keeps the old path.
- An animation shown in place is no longer taken for a still graphic (each of its frames was rasterized at its
  transform: about one rasterization per picture).
- NEON: the screen copy (RGB565 with dither), blending, the scaler's horizontal pass, bilinear resampling inside
  textures; the same pixels as the plain C code.
- ISAAC_GEN_FLAGS: extra compiler options for the generated game code; the FunKey's default "-O2 -mthumb": the code
  29% smaller and the game's logic 13% faster (17% with 10-19 enemies on screen).
- The BitmapData leaf cache 2 -> 6 MB on the FunKey (each room entry draws the room's floor and walls into its
  bitmap; most rooms now reuse the floor's), the renderer's cache 8 -> 4 MB. PlutoVG's coordinate rounding inline
  (roundf was a library call per point on ARMv7).
- Sound: 16-bit samples to FunKey-OS's default device (its route plugin converted every float sample); the mixer
  skips its cubic interpolation where it falls on a sample.
- Test hooks: ISAAC_SOFT_RASTERLOG covers rasterizations at a transform, ISAAC_SOFT_BMLOG (how often the bitmaps
  drawn change), ISAAC_LEAF_KB.
---
 CMakeLists.txt                                |  13 +
 rt/audio.cpp                                  |  25 +-
 rt/funkey.cpp                                 |  23 +-
 rt/platform.cpp                               |   8 +
 rt/render_soft.cpp                            | 304 ++++++++++++++----
 .../plutovg/source/plutovg-rasterize.c        |   5 +-
 6 files changed, 311 insertions(+), 67 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 954e6e3..e0fe3c3 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -138,6 +138,19 @@ add_library(isaacgen STATIC ${GEN_SRC})
 target_include_directories(isaacgen PRIVATE rt)
 # the generated code is huge: -O1 keeps compile times reasonable
 target_compile_options(isaacgen PRIVATE $<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:GNU,Clang>:-O1 -fno-strict-aliasing -w>)
+# options added after those for the generated code only (a later -O wins), e.g. "-O2 -mthumb". The FunKey (ARM):
+# -O2 in Thumb-2, the code 29% smaller and the game's logic 13% faster on the console than at -O1 in ARM mode (17% in
+# rooms with 10-19 enemies): that code mostly waits for memory, the instruction cache's included.
+if(ISAAC_FUNKEY AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "^arm")
+  set(ISAAC_GEN_FLAGS_DEFAULT "-O2 -mthumb")
+else()
+  set(ISAAC_GEN_FLAGS_DEFAULT "")
+endif()
+set(ISAAC_GEN_FLAGS "${ISAAC_GEN_FLAGS_DEFAULT}" CACHE STRING "extra compiler options for the generated game code")
+if(ISAAC_GEN_FLAGS)
+  separate_arguments(ISAAC_GEN_FLAGS_LIST UNIX_COMMAND "${ISAAC_GEN_FLAGS}")
+  target_compile_options(isaacgen PRIVATE ${ISAAC_GEN_FLAGS_LIST})
+endif()
 
